{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfh3oipxrq","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"BLOCKER: FeatureBench ON-arm KB cannot be generated as specified — onboard-loop has no judge flag and requires authored probes","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: The FB-3 handoff and docs/swe-bench-eval.md (line 86) say the self-learning KB variant is produced by \"onboard-loop.js with --judge enabled\". That flag does NOT exist anywhere in the codebase — onboard-loop.js, onboard-learn.js, onboard-harness.js have no --judge. There is exactly ONE onboarding pipeline: mine (onboard-mine-*) then agentic validate/keep (onboard-learn.js, which already filters to non-obvious notes) then export (export-kb.js). The only \"judge\" is onboard-harness.js's applied-correctness GRADER used in the MEASURE step to decide where to deepen — it does not toggle a second KB variant. So the two required blocks (plain vs selflearn) have no implemented mechanism to differ.\n\nSecond blocker: onboard-loop.js hard-exits (line 208) if no probes.json exists for the repo. onboard-probes.js is only a SCHEMA VALIDATOR, not a generator — probes must be hand-authored per repo. None of the 5 pilot repos (pandas, astropy, sphinx, seaborn, sympy) have probes, and the handoff never mentions authoring them. So the loop cannot run unattended on these foreign repos regardless of the variant question.\n\nThe deterministic pilot manifest (deliverable 1) WAS produced and is solid; deliverable 2 (the two KB variants) is blocked on the above design gap.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T17:14:28.705Z","vec":[-0.08440208435058594,-0.052985429763793945,-0.06348173320293427,0.002851417986676097,0.05379674956202507,-0.04632838815450668,0.03952570632100105,0.013711588457226753,-0.02229207009077072,0.02791464515030384,0.025886423885822296,-0.055288009345531464,-0.012382138520479202,-0.02251788228750229,-0.03971811383962631,0.04939621686935425,0.03739502653479576,-0.06270839273929596,-0.03189387917518616,0.027805